<Layout title="CV — Adam Morris">
  <article class="container detail">
    <a class="text-link cv-back" href={`${base}#background`}>← Back to background</a>
    <div class="cv-header"><h1>Adam Morris</h1><a class="button primary print-button" href={`${base}Adam-Morris-CV.pdf`} download>Download PDF ↗</a></div>
    <p class="lead">Robotics & Engineering PhD Researcher</p><p>Bristol, UK · <a href="mailto:adamrhysmorris@gmail.com">adamrhysmorris@gmail.com</a></p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/ks20447">GitHub</a> · <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/adam-morris-eng-maths/">LinkedIn</a> · <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&amp;user=NnjMzeMAAAAJ">Google Scholar</a></p>
    <p class="placeholder-note">Project details are placeholders and will be added shortly.</p>
    <section class="detail-section"><h2>Profile</h2><p>Engineering Mathematics PhD researcher investigating robot swarms for RF monitoring and concealed-emitter localisation, with relevance to defence and security. Combines simulation and robotic platforms with experience in AI consultancy, technical reporting and student supervision.</p></section>
    <section class="detail-section"><h2>Education</h2><h3>PhD in Engineering Mathematics</h3><p>University of Bristol · 2024–2028 (expected)</p><p>Thesis: Swarm-Enabled Spatial Intelligence</p><p>My PhD investigates how teams of autonomous robots can monitor and maintain the RF domain in secure environments, including localising anomalous signals from concealed adversarial transmitters.</p><p>I combine 2D simulations for swarm design, high-fidelity 3D electromagnetic propagation modelling, and ROS 2/Gazebo for robot-control simulation. I also work with physical robotic platforms, including the LEO Rover and Clearpath Jackal.</p><br/><h3>MEng in Engineering Mathematics</h3><p>University of Bristol · 2020–2024</p><p>First Class Honours</p><p>Dissertation: “Anti-aligning robots”</p></section>
    <section class="detail-section"><h2>Experience</h2><h3>Consultant Engineer</h3><p>SportsViz · June 2023–present · Part-time, remote</p><p>Researching novel data interpretation and artificial intelligence methods for elite sports performance analysis, in a project with the Football Association of Wales (FAW).</p><ul class="experience-points"><li>Authored technical reports reviewing the literature and setting out potential future research directions.</li><li>Demonstrated AI and data analysis capabilities for international-level sports performance analysis, engaging with clients from varied professional backgrounds.</li></ul><br/><h3>Graduate Teaching Support</h3><p>University of Bristol · September 2023–present</p><p>Support undergraduate and master’s students across a range of units and assignments.</p><ul class="experience-points"><li>Provide academic support in technical writing and research methodologies, including marking and one-to-one supervision of a master’s dissertation.</li><li>Quickly develop an understanding of unfamiliar topics to support student work, and coordinate meetings across multiple student groups.</li></ul></section>
